Dear Users,

	i have some difficulties in reading a function which is already in a 
function. I have created a lot of functions which interacts each other. 
Here as an example,

1. first i typed at the '>' prompt :> fix(my)

2. in the notepad editor i wrote :

function(t)

{

	eq1 <- function(x)

	{

		x^2

	}

	eq2 <- function(y)

	{

		eq1(y) + 2 * eq1(y)

	}

	cat(eq2(t), "\n")

}

3. then i run it by typing :> my(10)

    ** it comes to an error stating 'Error in eq2(t): couldn't find 
function "eq1"'

i found this structure is quite different from C/Pascal language i learned 
before:

here is an equality in pascal term which may help to explain what i'm going 
to achieve:

Uses Crt;
function my(t:byte):byte;
  function eq1(x:byte):byte;
   begin
    eq1:=x*x;
   end;
  function eq2(y:byte):byte;
   begin
     eq2:=eq1(y)+2*eq1(y);
   end;
begin
 may:=eq2(t);
end;

BEGIN {This is main program}
 Writeln(may(10));
END.

Would you mind helping me solve this problem?
Thanks Very Much.

Regards,

